  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 804.03 Sludge Quality Certification Required",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 804.03 Sludge Quality Certification Required.\n\n(a) Except as provided in (b) and (c) below, no person shall land apply, distribute for land application, sell, or give away any sludge or sludge mixture, in bulk, that is not covered by a sludge quality certification pursuant to Env-Wq 809.\n\n(b) An additional sludge quality certification shall not be required for a sludge mixture produced at a facility where each constituent sludge has a sludge quality certification and any other constituent is a non-sludge material.\n\n(c) A sludge quality certification shall not be required for sludge that is not used for land application.\n\nSource. #10998, eff 1-1-16; ss by #14571, eff 5-15-26, EXPIRES: 5-15-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq800.html"
